1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,990
Critical security alert for Windows Remote Desktop Licensing services. Active exploits weaponize zero-day vulnerability CVE-2024-38077.

2
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:25,800
Unauthenticated attackers trigger a heap buffer overflow in termsrv.dll over network port 135, gaining complete SYSTEM privileges.

3
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:37,100
Ransomware affiliates are utilizing automated scanners to locate internet-exposed RPC ports and execute rapid domain compromise.

4
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:49,770
Security operations must immediately monitor for abnormal inbound traffic on TCP Port 135 and block known adversary command infrastructure.

5
00:00:49,770 --> 00:01:00,490
All enterprise servers with Remote Desktop Licensing roles enabled are subject to immediate pre-auth compromise without user interaction.

6
00:01:00,490 --> 00:01:12,100
Immediately block TCP Port 135 at perimeter firewalls and disable public exposure of Remote Desktop Licensing services.

7
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:24,140
Emergency update KB5040442 resolves the heap overflow. Prioritize deployment to all external-facing Windows servers tonight.

8
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:36,260
Deploy endpoint detection rules to inspect svchost process integrity and flag suspicious child process creation from termsrv.dll.

9
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:48,260
If anomalous traffic on Port 135 is detected, immediately isolate affected hosts and initiate full enterprise forensic collection.

10
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:59,750
Executive mandate: all systems must complete mitigation within twenty-four hours. Report status to the CISO emergency operations desk.
